    "bounding box" : [ 179.64, 592.109, 432.233, 602.072 ],
    "font" : "CMCSC10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Appendix B. Measure-preserving diffeomorphisms"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 13,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 126.72, 537.75, 489.661, 584.192 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Let (M,g) be a smooth connected, orientable Riemannian manifold with Riemannian volume measure volg. We collect here some auxiliary results about the group Diﬀ+0 (g) of all compactly non-identical, orientation-preserving, volg-preserving diﬀeomorphisms."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 14,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 126.721, 501.869, 485.476, 537.91 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Firstly, let us recall that Diﬀ+0 (g) is the (inﬁnite-dimensional) Lie group corresponding to the Lie algebra of divg-free vector ﬁelds on M with the Lie derivative as its Lie bracket. Let us further recall some virtually well-known results about the"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 15,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 126.721, 477.869, 435.239, 502.03 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "natural action of Diﬀ+0 (g) on M. The following may be easily inferred from the arguments in [13, §3]."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 16,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 126.72, 435.056, 485.332, 469.592 ],
    "font" : "CMTI10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Lemma B.1 (Extension lemma). Let (M,g) be in addition open or boundaryless, and K ⊂ M be any contractible compact subset. Then, every smooth vector ﬁeld on K has a compactly supported, divg-free extension to the whole of M."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 17,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 126.72, 367.116, 486.632, 427.352 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "As an immediate consequence, we see that the Lie algebra of divg-free vector ﬁelds is inﬁnite-dimensional, thus so is Diﬀ+0 (g). Proposition B.2 (Transitivity, [13, Thm. A, §3, p. 98]). Diﬀ+0 (g) acts k-transitively on M for every k ∈ N1. In particular, it acts transitively on M."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 18,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 126.719, 343.256, 485.398, 367.27 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "B.1. Actions on measures. In the following, let B1 ⊂ Rd be the open unit ball equipped with the standard Euclidean metric ge."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 19,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 126.719, 305.916, 485.239, 335.552 ],
    "font" : "CMTI10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Lemma B.3. Let ν be any ﬁnite measure on B1 invariant for the ( ♯)-action of Diﬀ+0 (ge). Then ν ∝ L d B"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 21,
    "level" : "1",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 260.16, 312.989, 479.089, 322.952 ],
    "font" : "CMTI10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : ". In particular, ν has no singular continuous part."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 20,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 255.72, 309.315, 259.107, 314.296 ],
    "font" : "CMR5",
    "font size" : 4.981,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "1"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 22,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 126.719, 257.217, 485.34, 304.001 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Proof. Let Q1,Q2 ⊂ B1 be arbitrary closed cubes with equal volume, deﬁne K as the closed convex hull of Q1 ∪ Q2, and let w be the vector ﬁeld on K deﬁning the translation of Q1 to Q2. By Lemma B.1 applied to K and w, there exists a compactly supported divg"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 24,
    "level" : "2",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 126.719, 190.356, 485.408, 269.23 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "-free vector ﬁeld w′ on M extending w on K. Then, the ﬂow of w′ at time 1 is a compactly non-identical orientation-preserving, L dpreserving diﬀeomorphism on M mapping Q1 to Q2. In other words, Diﬀ+0 (ge) acts transitively on all closed cubes in B1, hence, by continuity, on the family C of all semi-closed cubes Q of the form Q := x + q [0,1)d with x ∈ Rd, q ∈ Q+ and such that Q ⊂ B1."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 23,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 240.96, 256.914, 244.332, 261.577 ],
    "font" : "CMMI5",
    "font size" : 4.981,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "e"
  }, {
    "type" : "image",
    "pdfua_tag" : "Figure",
    "id" : 25,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 148.188, 207.948, 156.108, 208.428 ],
    "alt_source" : "missing",
    "source" : "2503.07802_pg90_images/imageFile1.png"
  }, {
    "type" : "caption",
    "pdfua_tag" : "Caption",
    "id" : 26,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 126.72, 131.697, 485.52, 195.761 ],
    "linked content id" : 25,
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Since ν is invariant, by a standard decomposition argument, for every rational q ∈ Q+ and every Q ∈ C with qQ ∈ C we have ν(qQ) = qdνQ. Now, let Q0 ∈ C be ﬁxed, and set c := νQ0/L dQ0. For every Q1 ∈ C there exists q ∈ Q+ and x ∈ Rd so that Q1 = x+qQ0. For such q, by invariance of ν and of L d (also under rescaling), νQ1 = ν(qQ0) = qdνQ0 = qdcL dQ0 = cL d(qQ0) = cL dQ1 ."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 27,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 126.721, 91.589, 485.409, 125.801 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Since C is a π-system generating the Borel σ-algebra of B1, it follows by a standard monotone class argument that ν = cL d as Borel measures on B1, which concludes the proof."
  } ]
}